    {
      "text": "\"Overwhelming.\" This is the title of Sura 88. In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful. [88:1] Are you aware of the Overwhelming? [88:2] Faces on that day will be shamed. [88:3] Laboring and exhausted. [88:4] Suffering in a blazing Hellfire. [88:5] Drinking from a flaming spring. [88:6] They will have no food except the useless variety. [88:7] It never nourishes, nor satisfies hunger. [88:8] Other faces on that day will be full of joy. [88:9] Satisfied with their work. [] In an exalted Paradise. [] In it, no nonsense is heard. [] In it, a spring flows. [] In it, there are luxurious furnishings. [] And drinks made available. [] And pitchers in rows. [] And carpets throughout. [88:1] Are you aware of the Overwhelming? This is another word or term that is used in the Quran to describe the Day of Judgment. We've seen in the previous Suras. I think we can go back, even though we have done it probably two weeks ago. I can quickly go back to Sura 82, 81. I think 81 and 82 started with the description of the Day of Judgment. 82 says, [82:1] When the heaven is shattered. [82:2] The planets are scattered. [82:3] The oceans are exploded. [82:4] The graves are opened. [82:5] Every soul will find out what caused it to advance, and what caused it to regress. Similar expression in Sura 81. [81:1] When the sun is rolled. [81:2] The stars are crashed into each other. [81:3] The mountains are wiped out. [81:4] The reproduction is halted. [81:5] The beasts are summoned. [81:6] The oceans are set aflame. These are all overwhelming. I mean, these are heavy events.",
