    {
      "text": "When I served in Saudi Arabia for the United Nations, I came across a daily program where people send messages, and most of these messages were from women. I'm telling you, I cried. I actually cried listening to that program. Because a typical story will be a woman whose husband disappeared for six months or a year. She doesn't know where he is. She's grounded in the apartment or the house or the place that's assigned for her. Dr. Rashad Khalifa thanks God for the freedom in America to practise following Quran alone. And her in-laws bring whatever food or whatever that keeps her alive. She never leaves the place. It's just like a prison. And this is a typical story. And she's asking for help. Obviously she snuck out a letter to that radio program.",
